{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-17_17-50-22-hashicorp_raft-real-run && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\ns=json.load(open('state.json'))\ncur=[i for i in s['interpretations'] if i['id'].startswith('caa518ff')][0]\nkn={k['id']:k for k in s['knowledge']}\n\npara=(\\\"Question-level consolidation after the premise correction. The verification entry now records that verifyLeader starts the count at one for the leader itself, sizes a voter-only quorum and registers the future on every replication stream. Read across both lineages that this account uses, that arithmetic explains every recorded outcome: in the five-member receipts the quorum is two, the leader supplies one vote and a single non-voter acknowledgement completes the verification, and the control with the non-voters also cut has no second acknowledgement and fails after about a second; in the lease receipts the same shape succeeds at the first attempt under both a 500 ms and a 1 s lease and then fails when the lease-driven step-down arrives, at 510 ms and 1018 ms; in the end-to-end receipts the same first verification succeeds at 0 ms while the successor commits only after about 2.4 seconds, and the later verification is refused because the node is no longer the leader. Nothing above depends on the leader being excluded from the count, so the correction sharpens the mechanism without changing the conclusion that the verification is satisfied without a second voter.\\\")\n\nans={\n \\\"1e9081120a23413eaaf020fffb085a1b-gap-0\\\":{\n  \\\"explanation\\\":\\\"The current explanation and the lease experiment, both of which this question-level account carries, assert only that a verification succeeds while one of three voters is reachable and the non-voters answer. With the leader's self-vote recorded, that is exactly a quorum of two met by the leader plus one non-voter acknowledgement, so the affected uses are confirmed rather than revised; their recorded comparison results stay violated.\\\",\n  \\\"resolved\\\": True},\n \\\"1e9081120a23413eaaf020fffb085a1b-gap-1\\\":{\n  \\\"explanation\\\":\\\"The end-to-end receipts from 2fd5794c550141f7889f1530295d1294-experiment, 27d9e2e68fcf4e15b00b170ef9593714 and its repeat fb14e70f60a3456eae7774eb6e005e69, are cited in this question-level record. They recorded a first verification succeeding at 0 ms under the same three-voter quorum, which the corrected premise explains the same way, and a later verification refused because the node had stepped down; neither observation depended on how the two votes were supplied, so those receipts need no reinterpretation and the bound they measured stands.\\\",\n  \\\"resolved\\\": True},\n}\n\nupd={\n \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Close the two gaps opened by the VerifyLeader premise correction with a question-level explanation that spans the experiment lineages involved. The correction adds the leader's self-vote, which makes the quorum arithmetic explicit across the five-member, lease-varied and end-to-end receipts alike; the explanation keeps the asserted defect claim and the violated comparison results those receipts recorded.\\\",\n \\\"interpretations\\\":[{\n  \\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"533b966489544f45b4fcf14f6edce57f-question-0\\\",\n  \\\"experiment_id\\\":None,\n  \\\"source_ids\\\":cur['source_ids'],\n  \\\"executions\\\":{\\\"871eb51d712b4c269dd592937ab068f7\\\":[0,1,2,3],\\\"fb14e70f60a3456eae7774eb6e005e69\\\":[0,1,2,3]},\n  \\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"explained\\\",\n  \\\"defect_claim\\\":\\\"asserted\\\",\n  \\\"rationale\\\":cur['rationale']+\\\"\\\\n\\\\n\\\"+para,\n  \\\"counterevidence\\\":cur['counterevidence'],\n  \\\"limitations\\\":cur['limitations'],\n  \\\"joint_history\\\":cur['joint_history'],\n  \\\"answers\\\":ans,\n  \\\"knowledge\\\":[\n   {\\\"entry_id\\\":\\\"533b966489544f45b4fcf14f6edce57f-knowledge-0\\\",\\\"revision\\\":kn['533b966489544f45b4fcf14f6edce57f-knowledge-0']['revision'],\\\"assertion\\\":\\\"verifyLeader arms the verification with the leader's own vote, sizes the quorum by voters and registers the future on every replication stream, so with three voters one non-voter acknowledgement completes it.\\\"},\n   {\\\"entry_id\\\":\\\"533b966489544f45b4fcf14f6edce57f-knowledge-1\\\",\\\"revision\\\":kn['533b966489544f45b4fcf14f6edce57f-knowledge-1']['revision'],\\\"assertion\\\":\\\"checkLeaderLease counts only voters, unlike VerifyLeader.\\\"},\n  ],\n }],\n}\njson.dump(upd, open('draft/update.json','w'), indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)\nopen('draft/update.json','a').write('\\\\n')\nprint('written')\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -c \\\"\nimport json,jsonschema\ns=json.load(open('/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-17_17-50-22-hashicorp_raft-real-run/submission.schema.json'))\nd=json.load(open('/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-17_17-50-22-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft/update.json'))\njsonschema.validate(d,s);i=d['interpretations'][0]\nprint('schema OK ce=',len(i['counterevidence']),'lim=',len(i['limitations']),'exp=',i['experiment_id'],'execs=',list(i['executions']))\\\"\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
